      "name": "Verdier's Division",
      "formation": "8th Division, II Corps (Oudinot)",
      "side": "French",
      "summary": "Joined Legrand at Yakubovo late on 30 July and shared the defeat next day. On 1 August, as Oudinot turned at Boyarshchina, it caught Kulnev's pursuing advance guard coming out of the woods and broke it, and then held off Wittgenstein's counter-attack at Golovchitsy.",
      "notes": [
        "After Nafziger: sixteen battalions, about 10,000 men. The 124th was a Dutch regiment, raised from the old Dutch army.",
        "Nafziger (after Fabry) gives each regiment its artillery company, two or four 3-pdrs, shown as Regimental Artillery; he notes it isn't certain they were with their regiments in the field.",
        "Pouget's brigade mixes a regimental battery (the 37th's four guns) with a section (the 124th's two), and the horse battery has none of the three cavalry regiments the list wants for it; both show as historical departures.",
